<!--
  EXAMPLE CLAUDE.md — a lean, one-page repo instruction file for an AI coding agent.
  Copy into your repo root as CLAUDE.md and replace every ‹fill in›.
  Read the guide (README.md next to this file) for WHY each section exists.

  Rule of thumb: every line is either a FACT the agent can't guess,
  or a rule tied to a failure you have ACTUALLY watched it make. Delete the rest.
  Verify each command runs before committing it — a wrong command here is worse than none.
  Never put secrets, tokens, or production hostnames here — this file ships every session.
-->

# Commands
- Test:    ‹make test›        (single: ‹make test FILTER=Foo›)
- Check:   ‹make check›       # lint + types + format + static analysis + tests, one gate
- Format:  ‹make fmt›
- Done = `make check` passes on touched files + summary notes any API/schema/config change.

# Structure
- ‹src/services›   — business logic lives here, not in controllers/handlers
- ‹src/models›     — data contracts / types; reuse before creating new ones
- ‹src/lib›        — shared helpers and utilities; reuse before adding
- ‹migrations/›    — never edit an existing migration; add a new one
- ‹legacy/›        — change with extra care (see Safety)

# Code changes
- Reuse existing types, models, helpers, and services. Adding a new
  package/pattern/abstraction: name what you checked first and why it didn't fit.
- Follow surrounding code style even if imperfect.
- Fix only what the task requires. Note unrelated problems at the end; don't fix them.
- Legacy code: optimize for safety and compatibility first.

# Safety
- Do not change public APIs, routes, database schema, configs, or permissions unless required.
  If a change touches any of these, call it out at the top of your summary.
- Never paste code, credentials, or private data into web searches or external tools.

# Communication
- Be practical, concise, terse.
- Unclear task: make the best reasonable assumption and state it in one line.
- Ask only when continuing may cause a wrong or destructive change.
- Schema / API / auth / multi-file changes: list Risks + Assumptions before implementing.
  Label Verified / Assumed only when they differ. Trivial changes: just do them.
- Prefer the smallest relevant verification or spike first.

# Local & shared
- If `AGENTS.local.md` exists, follow it: @AGENTS.local.md
- Shared cross-tool knowledge lives in AGENTS.md: @AGENTS.md
- Search with `rg` / `fd`, not `grep -R` / `find`.
